Ten minutes later, a woman comes to the counter.
She orders a cappuccino.
My first coffee did not turn out well earlier.
Now I am making my second coffee.
I take a deep breath.
Elif said I have to learn to be patient.
I think of everything she has shown me.
This time, the espresso does not run too fast.
Then I froth the milk.
I watched closely how Elif did that.
The milk is creamy and looks good.
I pour it carefully into the cup.
"Here is your cappuccino," I say to the woman.
The woman takes the cup and smiles.
I am really very relieved.
I am slowly learning to make good coffee.
Elif comes to me and nods.
"You made that great," she says.
